        "id": 1002186
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-10T07:19:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Suggestion: We can use `std::expected\u003cstd::string,uint16_t\u003e` as the return type. In success path, the expanded location code will be returned and on failure error code will be returned. This avoids returning unexpanded location code in error path and makes the return value more usable to the caller.",
      "revId": "9bda0c0f0a057bf552e95bedc09e7d5514ae0eb9",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d08e3183_625199db",
        "filename": "vpd-manager/include/utility/vpd_specific_utility.hpp",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 1521,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000353
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-10T13:22:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Based on use cases here, we don\u0027t treat  failure error code  as a blocker.\ncaller uses returned data(expanded/unexpanded) directly.  if error code !\u003d 0 then log a message.\nIf we go with std::expected\u003cstd::string,uint16_t\u003e, we need special handling here-\nIn good case- use returned data, in error case- use what input was given.\nI think current design is simpler.",
      "parentUuid": "0bf9ab55_efc08799",
      "revId": "9bda0c0f0a057bf552e95bedc09e7d5514ae0eb9",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "472d30a2_8e638d3b",
        "filename": "vpd-manager/include/utility/vpd_specific_utility.hpp",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 1521,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002186
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-15T07:15:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003eif error code !\u003d 0 then log a message.\n\nWe can do that with `std::expected\u003c\u003e` as well.\n\n\u003eIf we go with std::expected\u003cstd::string,uint16_t\u003e, we need special handling here-\nIn good case- use returned data, in error case- use what input was given.\n\nI do not see what \"special handling\" is required here?\n\n\u003eI think current design is simpler. \n\nThat\u0027s subjective. But passing output parameters by reference and then reading them is C styled code and not in line with modern C++. It puts more burden on the caller to create an error code variable.",
      "parentUuid": "d08e3183_625199db",
      "revId": "9bda0c0f0a057bf552e95bedc09e7d5514ae0eb9",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
